Org members hold one of five roles, in order: viewer, member, reviewer,
admin, owner. The org role applies to every project; a project role can raise
it for one project ('lorvik project member'). Removing a member revokes their
tokens. Members are addressed by actor id, or user:<id> and agent:<id>; a bare
id means a user. You cannot grant a role above your own.

Examples:
  lorvik member ls
  lorvik member add 106666050296328877 --role member
  lorvik member role 106666050296328877 reviewer
  lorvik member remove 106666050296328877

Usage
  lorvik member [flags]
  lorvik member [command]

Commands
  add         Add an org member
  ls          List org members
  remove      Remove an org member and revoke their tokens
  role        Change an org member's role

Flags
  -h, --help   help for member

Global flags
      --api-url string   Server URL (default: LORVIK_API_URL)
      --json             Output the raw API JSON
  -p, --project string   Project slug (default: LORVIK_PROJECT or .lorvik.toml)
  -Q, --quiet            Suppress the unread notice on stderr and an empty inbox
      --session string   Session label for this chat (default: LORVIK_SESSION or derived; see lorvik session)

Run 'lorvik member <command> --help' for more information about a command.
